# Paths that live in the repository but must NEVER reach the public server.
#
# This file exists because the repository is becoming the publishing
# vehicle rather than a backup of it. Under the old rsync-by-hand model a
# human named what to send, so internal files were safe by omission.
# Once a tag deploys the tree, omission is no longer protection: every
# tracked file is a candidate for publication unless it is listed here.
#
# rsync --exclude-from syntax. Directories need a trailing slash.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
docs/
tools/
tmp/
_drafts/
*.bak-*
*.bak-preayllu
CLAUDE.md
.deployignore
.gitignore
.mcp.json
